{{also|bauer}}
==English==

===Etymology===
* As a German and Jewish surname, from {{bor|en|de|Bauer|t=farmer}}. Compare {{m|en|Bower}}.
* Also as a German and Jewish surname, from the obsolete {{der|en|gmh|-}} noun {{m|gmh|(ge)būr|t=neighbor}}, from {{der|en|goh|bur|t=dwelling}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈbaʊ.əɹ/|/ˈbaʊəɹ/|a=UK}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-bower.wav|Audio (Southern England)}}
* {{rhymes|en|aʊ.ə(ɹ)|aʊə(ɹ)|s1=2}}
* {{homophones|en|Bower|bower}} {{q|some etymologies}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{surname|en|from=German}}.

====Statistics====
* According to the 2010 United States Census, ''Bauer'' is the 517<sup>th</sup> most common surname in the United States, belonging to 65,004 individuals. ''Bauer'' is most common among White (95.1%) individuals.

